<title>GREECE: IONIAN BANK CUTS DEPOSIT, LENDING RATES.</title>
<headline>IONIAN BANK CUTS DEPOSIT, LENDING RATES.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>State Ionian Bank will</p>
<p>cut its deposit and lending rates by 50 basis points, effective</p>
<p>September 16, it said in a statement. Its new rate structure</p>
<p>will have as follows:</p>
<p>WORKING CAPITAL LOANS</p>
<p>    Base lending rate:	 18.50  from 19.00 percent</p>
<p>Preferred lending rate:  stays unchanged at 17.00 percent</p>
<p>FIXED ASSET LOANS</p>
<p>    Base lending rate:	 18.50 from 19.00 percent</p>
<p>    Mortgages:		   15.50 from 16.00 percent</p>
<p>    Consumer Loans:	    23.50 from 24.00 percent</p>
<p>DEPOSIT RATES</p>
<p>    Savings deposit:	   11.50 from 12.00 percent</p>
<p>Time deposits for amounts up to 25 million drachmas will</p>
<p>have as follows:</p>
<p>    3-months:		    12.50 from 13.25 percent</p>
<p>    6-months:		    12.75 from 13.50 percent</p>
<p>    9-months:		    12.75 from 13.50 percent</p>
<p>    12-months:		   13.00 from 13.75 percent</p>
<p>Deposit rates for amounts over 25 million drachmas are</p>
<p>negotiable, it said.</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
